  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transportation Routes to and from Ca&#xE0;la Logistical Platform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the construction of the Ca&#xE0;la Logistical Platform (CLP) in Angola. The goal is to decrease post-harvest losses and boost the sector&#x2019;s robustness and competitiveness by developing efficient transport lines to and from the CLP. The project includes mapping transport routes within a 150 km perimeter of the CLP, optimizing both truck and rail transport to the port of Lobito, and analyzing the associated economic costs. Key activities involve identifying major production and storage hubs, assessing transport resources, and ensuring proper cold chain management. By creating detailed maps and models, the project will facilitate better planning and implementation of transportation solutions, ultimately reducing post-harvest losses and improving market access.</narrative>
  </description>
